<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cape Verde</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cape Verde is an archipelago in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, uninhabited until Portuguese settlement in the fifteenth century. It became an important base for Atlantic shipping and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. The islands remained a colony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> until independence in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cape-verde.jpg" alt="Cape Verde" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Pedro Gregório Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Cape_Verde_(3-2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
